    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), derived at creation from the owner's own fields.\n\n**1. `model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced `getMembershipTier()` (which returned `GOLD`/`SILVER`/`BRONZE` off `householdSize`, email, and namesakes) with `getMembershipLevel()`:\n```java\nint level = 1;\nif (hasEmail) level++;            // +1 when an email is present\nif (noNamesakes) level++;         // +1 when namesakeCount == 0\nreturn Math.min(level, 3);        // cap at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure)\n```\n\n**2. `resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Swapped the `membershipTier` response property (string) for `membershipLevel` (`integer`, `int32`, min 1 / max 3). This is what regenerates `OwnerDto`, so the field is removed from the response in favour of the new one; MapStruct maps `getMembershipLevel` \u2192 `setMembershipLevel` by name automatically.\n\n**3. `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel={}` (the thing that recorded tier behaviour now records the level), and I removed a now-defunct javadoc reference to the old `GOLD` tier.\n\n## Notes on judgment calls\n- The existing create audit line didn't literally contain a tier token, but the spec said \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead\", so I made the audit line record `membershipLevel` to satisfy that intent. No test asserts audit content, so this is additive and safe.\n- `householdSize` is still computed/stored but no longer feeds the level (the old `GOLD` behaviour is gone, as the new formula defined). It isn't exposed in the API, so I left the field in place.\n\n## Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The acceptance test `coreNumericLevel` (email present + unique name \u2192 level `1+1+1` capped at `3`) passes, and the audit log confirms `membershipLevel=3`.",
